    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d325">

                <pb facs="0458" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg388"/>

                <head>Mr. Dayton to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 193.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-09-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 12, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Agreeably to your directions in despatch
                    No. 201, I informed Mr. Thouvenel to-day of the circumstances under which the
                    Mexican government had negotiated certain drafts upon the United States, based
                    on treaties negotiated by Mr. Corwin and not ratified by our government, and
                    which drafts were therefore unpaid.</p>
                <p>Mr. Thouvenel, it would seem, had not seen the subject referred to in the public
                    journals. He expressed his appreciation of the attention and friendship of the
                    United States in the action of the government and in making the communication
                    above referred to.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM L. DAYTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi><hi
                            rendition="#italic"> Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.,</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
